  "text": "Dreams held deep meaning in Celtic religion. They gave access to the Otherworld. The aisling is a traditional Irish poem in which the poet met supernatural beings in a dreaming state. Fairy people visited human dreamers. The fairy queen Fand seduced the hero Cúchulainn in this way. An unnamed fairy of a western isle lured Bran mac Febail to her realm. One divination rite used this belief. In the tarbhfleis, or bull-sleep, a bard ate the meat of a newly killed bull. He slept wrapped in the bloody hide. Then he dreamed the name of the next king.",
